WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.868
-Our next guests
are both talented actresses

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.303
and real-life sisters
whose new films,

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:06.739
"Sister Swap:
A Hometown Holiday"

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.841
and "Sister Swap:
Christmas in the City,"

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.343
are a part of Hallmark Channel's
Countdown to Christmas.

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:13.179
Let's take a look.
-I was thinking,

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:16.048
what if I didn't go back
to Hazelwood?

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:17.683
-I think that's really smart.

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.819
-You don't think Mom and Dad
are going to be upset

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.954
if I stay here
for a couple more days?

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:25.024
-I think they'd be glad
you're trying something new.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:29.261
-Oh. Sister swap! I love this!

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:30.763
-I do, too. Alright.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.565
I'm going to tell Joe
that you're helping out, okay?

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:35.134
-Oh, no, no. Let me.
I can handle it.

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:37.303
-Okay. Alright.
Well, um, I love you.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.371
Call me if anything
comes up, okay?

00:00:39.371 --> 00:00:41.808
-I promise I will.
I love you, too.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.009
-Bye.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:45.812
-Also I'm never
giving back this coat.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.147
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.450
Kimberly Williams-Paisley
and Ashley Williams!

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.985
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.985 --> 00:01:00.259
♪♪

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:07.533
♪♪

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.602
-Yeah!
-Welcome back, ladies!

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.836
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.105
-Thank you.
-We're really happy to be here.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.406
-We're so happy to be here.
-I want to clean up

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.907
a little bit,
as quickly as I can,

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.509
the weird way
we all know each other.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.877
-Yeah.
-My sister-in-law

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.580
knows your husband,
and through that connection,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.850
you called your sister, who's
husbands with Brad Paisley,

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.052
who then agreed to play --

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.386
-Husband's wife.
-Yes, he's your husband.

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:28.521
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.990
I think it's so nice
that you guys swap that.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.291
You're like, "We don't --
We're not --

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:33.759
We don't care what it is."

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:34.927
-We're not into labels.
-Yeah.

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:37.130
So your husband, Brad Paisley,

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.699
then came and surprised my wife
at our wedding.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.433
-With me. I came, too.
-With you.

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:43.068
You came, as well.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:43.068 --> 00:01:45.038
-Also, you and I -- Also, you
and I went to college together.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.439
-We did.
-But we did not know each other.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.907
And you were
the first famous person

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.609
I saw in person,
because when you were in college

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.244
you had already been
in "Father of the Bride."

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.778
-Holy cow.
-I'm exhausted.

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:54.413
-You just did that.
-Are you guys okay?

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:56.216
-We know each other
a lot of different ways.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.650
-Yeah, we do. We do. We do.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.987
-And then one of the craziest
things happened, is my wife

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.588
and I came to Nashville
to see you and Brad.

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:04.924
-Mm-hmm.
-And you guys --

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.926
Brad came over to the hotel.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.394
You came separately.
-We came separately.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.162
-And then you drove home
in one car.

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:12.431
-Right. And I left my car.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:15.268
And I said, "You guys
come visit the farm tomorrow

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.902
and just bring my car home."

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:19.371
-Yep.
-And then you stole the car.

00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:21.808
-Okay.
-Okay. Back it up.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.643
-This is not really true. But --

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.177
-I mean, it is.
That's what happened.

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:26.613
-We went down to the valet

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.081
and said, "We're here
for Kimberly's car."

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.615
-Yeah. Yeah, I gave you
my valet ticket.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:30.816
-You gave us a ticket.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:32.084
-So we gave the ticket.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:33.520
-And then my wife texted you.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.755
-And she said,
"I love your Porsche."

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.356
-Yeah.

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:42.594
-And I drive
a Chevy SUV mom car.

00:02:42.594 --> 00:02:45.865
I wrote back, "Ha ha.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.167
LOL."

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.501
And she -- Wait. Wait.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.672
She wrote back and went,
"Uh, you don't have a Porsche?"

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.240
And I said,
"No, I don't have a Porsche."

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.844
And then you guys were like, at,
breakfast with the nice Porsche.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.812
-Yeah.
-And I wish I was that person

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.848
that you thought I was
for a second.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.315
-The most embarrassing thing

00:03:03.315 --> 00:03:05.284
was then I had to
drive a Porsche

00:03:05.284 --> 00:03:08.954
that I now knew I had stolen...
-Right.

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.790
-...back to a hotel
without crashing it.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.391
-Yeah.
-And then there were a few --

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:13.993
I realize a bunch
of clues I missed.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.361
-Yeah.
-Which is, when Alexi got in,

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.797
there was, like, a pair
of size-14 shoes and, like --

00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:22.101
And when I had gotten in,
I had to move the seat way up.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.169
-Right, right. But that
could have been the valet.

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:25.905
-Could have been the valet.
That's true.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.539
-Yeah. And he left
his shoes in there?

00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:29.776
I don't know.
-But then it was nice that

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:32.278
when I went back and switched
and got your car, it was --

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.380
There was, like, half a salad.
-Right.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.614
It was -- That was obvious.

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:37.383
You were like, "Oh, this is Kim.
This makes sense."

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.017
There was, like, half a salad
in the front seat

00:03:39.017 --> 00:03:40.954
and NPR on the radio.

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:44.457
-I was like, "I can't believe we
thought the Porsche was hers."

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.724
-I can't either.

00:03:45.724 --> 00:03:47.593
-So you guys live
in different cities now.

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:49.661
You're in L.A.
You're in Nashville.

00:03:49.661 --> 00:03:50.930
And it must be so nice

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.732
to both be doing press
for this project together

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.801
and be back in New York
where you guys grew up.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:57.269
-We love being back here.
-It's amazing. Yeah.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:59.939
-And we are East Coast people,
through and through.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.975
And speaking of the East Coast,
Kim just had a big birthday.

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:05.945
-I did.
-And the big --

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.480
-It had to do with
where we're from.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.748
-Yeah.
-So let me back up.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:12.285
So, in sixth grade,
I went to P.S. 8 in Yonkers.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.519
-Okay.
-P.S. 8.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:16.722
And I was in love
with Frankie Dibona.

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:17.990
-Okay.
-He was my first crush.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.892
-Who wasn't, in Yonkers?
-Seriously.

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.161
Frankie was adorable.
He was my first crush.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.629
-So hot.
-And one day -- one day

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:27.399
in school he said, "I'm going
to kiss you after school."

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:30.803
And I was like, "Okay."
And --

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.739
-I do want to give everybody
a little visual of Frankie.

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.074
-That's Frankie!
-Frankie!

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.375
-That's Kim.
-That's Kim.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.177
-Okay, so Frankie --
-And that's Stacy.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.012
-And that's Plan B
in case you said no.

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:41.780
-Yes! Yes!

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.849
-"Frankie Dibona
has always got two options!"

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:46.485
-Yes. Yes. He did.
He had a few options.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:48.287
So he goes,
"I'm going to kiss you

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:49.655
for ten seconds after school."

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.457
And Stacy's like, "I'll count."

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.126
And so I was like, "Okay."

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.693
So at the end of the day,
I go outside,

00:04:54.693 --> 00:04:56.194
and there's Frankie
in the schoolyard

00:04:56.194 --> 00:04:57.863
eating Cheez Doodles.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:04:59.598
And he goes, "Are you ready?"

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.633
And I said, "But you're
eating Cheez Doodles."

00:05:01.633 --> 00:05:05.070
And he says, "It don't matter."

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.973
He goes, "It don't matter.
Not the way I kiss."

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:09.775
And then he goes like --

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:12.478
you know, like, smack kiss
for ten seconds.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:15.548
And Stacy goes,
"One, two, three..."

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:18.017
She was chewing gum.
She got all the way to ten.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.585
Happiest day of my life.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.587
So...
-So you knew then --

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.455
You knew this was a piece
of her personal history.

00:05:23.455 --> 00:05:25.557
-This story is family legacy
at this point, right?

00:05:25.557 --> 00:05:27.360
-Yeah, I mean,
kids quote Frankie Dibona.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.529
Everyone's like, "It don't
matter. It don't matter."

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:30.797
-"It don't matter."
-Yeah.

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:33.231
So I just decided
that, for Kim's birthday,

00:05:33.231 --> 00:05:36.235
I was going to get back
in touch with Frank Dibona.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.037
-Yes!
-'Cause --

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:42.442
I mean, what other option
was there for her birthday?

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:43.876
-Right, right.
-Sure.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:46.979
-So I googled every single
Frank Dibona in North America.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.881
-Right.
-And there are a lot.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.082
-Yeah.

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:52.151
-So I talked to somebody
in Seattle.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:53.652
I talked to somebody in Boston.

00:05:53.652 --> 00:05:56.455
-You were cold-calling Dibonas?
-Cold-calling Frankie Dibonas.

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:57.856
I talked to these people
in the Midwest

00:05:57.856 --> 00:06:00.192
who are still calling me.

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:03.462
So, finally,
I find Frank Dibona,

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:05.565
who happens to run
a very successful

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:08.100
auto-mechanic shop in Yonkers.
-Yeah.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:13.573
-And he answers the phone.
And he goes, "Yeah?"

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:17.342
And I was like, "Um, hi.
Is this Frank Dibona?

00:06:17.342 --> 00:06:21.347
Did you kiss a girl named
Kim Williams in sixth grade?"

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:23.816
And he goes,
"Who wants to know?"

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:26.585
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.585 --> 00:06:29.722
And I was like -- I was like,
"Oh, my gosh. I'm in."

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.524
I was like, "Hi, Frank.
My name is Ashley.

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:33.893
You don't know me. But my sister
has a big birthday.

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:35.828
And I was wondering
if I can convince you

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.863
to make a happy-birthday video

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:40.700
because she was in love
with you in sixth grade."

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:44.704
And he said, "Wait. Hold --
Hold on one second."

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:47.406
He goes, "Yeah, you tell
that lady with the Subaru

00:06:47.406 --> 00:06:49.375
that I'm not gonna
fix her bumper."

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.643
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.643 --> 00:06:53.713
So he comes back,
and I'm so nervous.

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:56.148
So I was like, "So, anyway.

00:06:56.148 --> 00:06:59.251
Can -- Can you make this happy
birthday video for my sister?"

00:06:59.251 --> 00:07:01.820
And he goes, "You know what?
I don't want no trouble.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.121
Like, who's her husband?

00:07:03.121 --> 00:07:05.792
Like, I don't want
to make anybody jealous."

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:08.294
And I was like --
-Clearly, he's not a fan.

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:12.064
Like, "I assure you
that her husband

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.100
is very confident
in his marriage."

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:19.939
And, uh, so, anyway, he made
this incredible, loving,

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:22.074
hilarious happy-birthday video
for my sister.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.110
And we couldn't be there
the night

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:27.646
that it was presented to you,
but I was there on FaceTime.

00:07:27.646 --> 00:07:32.084
And I think we have a photo
of the moment of the big reveal.

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.552
-This is so wonderful.

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:36.655
-So this is Kim sitting there.

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:41.393
-This is me, having nailed it.
And there is Kim.

00:07:41.393 --> 00:07:43.896
-Best birthday ever.
-I nailed her birthday.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:45.998
-Wow!

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:48.033
-So I just -- I also --
I just want to take

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:51.137
this opportunity to say hello,
Frankie Dibona.

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:52.471
-Yeah.
-We love you.

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:55.574
If anybody needs
some car repairs in Yonkers,

00:07:55.574 --> 00:07:56.909
-Look him up.
-please look him up.

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.444
And please watch
our Hallmark movie.

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:00.112
-Yeah. This is cool.

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:02.114
You're going to announce tonight
that you are, in fact,

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:03.449
leaving Brad for Frankie?

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:06.052
-No!
-No, no, no, no!

00:08:06.052 --> 00:08:07.486
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:10.622
-Well, let's not make news.
We'll be right back with more

00:08:10.622 --> 00:08:13.025
from Kimberly Williams-Paisley
and Ashley Williams.

